 "reading": {
  "the_armor_generalizes": "the four named armor modules (SbRomArmorSmm 51080191, PrepareWhiteListSmm 391626DB, FlashSmiSmm 6C289241, FlashSmiDxe 755877A6) ship under the SAME GUIDs on MSI (2023), Gigabyte (2026) and ASRock (2025) — the ASUS flash armor is an AMI-Aptio platform deliverable, not an ASUS customization; ASUS's own copies are GUID-found only (the nameplate blindness)",
  "one_guard_three_bodies": "SbRomArmorSmm has THREE distinct FFS bodies across four vendors — MSI and ASRock ship a byte-identical body (514b5bccf8e77f47), Gigabyte and ASUS each their own; the other three armor modules build one body per vendor (4/4 distinct) — the guard identity is AMI-generic, the bodies are vendor builds",
  "msi_carries_the_legacy": "MSI 7C02v3G1 (2023-03) still carries legacy-SMM-827E45A4 — coherent with the ring-18 retirement calendar (ASUS retired it at 4202, 2023-08, two months AFTER MSI's last release); the frozen cliff is visible inside the SMM layer too",
  "the_smm_spine": "42 SMM GUIDs sit in all five specimens (AMD family stacks AmdCcx*/AmdFabric*/AmdApcb*/AodSmm*, AMD FCH stacks FchSmmDispatcher per family, AMI plumbing Cf9ResetSmm/SmmPcieSataController/SmmGenericSio) — ring -2 is an AMD+AMI co-production; OVMF's SMM reference set overlaps each vendor by exactly 4 GUIDs (the EDK2-heritage core)",
  "msi_double_window": "MSI 7C02v3G1 counts 2x SMM-core and ships every armor GUID twice — the two complete SPI windows of ring 17, re-proven at SMM granularity; all set math dedupes per specimen"
 },
 "honesty": [
  "SMM membership is by PI file type (0x0A/0x0C/0x0D) — the same census the ring-19 register used; the two ASUS gates reproduce it exactly",
  "body identity is sha256 of the WHOLE FFS file body (all sections), not of the PE text — rebuild noise inside one section flips the hash without a semantic change",
  "MSI's double window double-counts per-occurrence numbers (files, named); all set operations dedupe — the first spine computation did NOT dedupe and fabricated an all-5 armor spine, caught by the variants probe before publication",
  "the corpus is the four latest-official specimens + one ASUS reference rung; an older MSI release could predate the armor entirely (the 2023-03 cliff sits INSIDE the armor era)",
  "armor presence on the other vendors is identity-level (GUID + body bytes); whether their SPI-protection POLICY matches ASUS's is a runtime question the image cannot answer"
 ]
}
